A JSON REST API for a small library: books, members and loans. It uses only Python's standard library: `http.server`, `sqlite3` and `json`.

## Requirements

- Python 3.10 or newer. Nothing else to install.

## Design

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `server.py` | Starts the API on http://127.0.0.1:8000 (this computer only) |
| `library_api/schema.sql` | Database tables: `books`, `members`, `loans` |
| `library_api/db.py` | Opens the SQLite database and creates the tables |
| `library_api/store.py` | Validation and all database work for books, members and loans |
| `library_api/api.py` | Routes each request to the right action and returns JSON |
| `tests/` | Unit tests for the storage rules and every endpoint |

**Rules the API enforces**

- Titles, authors, names and emails are required. An ISBN must have 10 or 13 digits and must be unique.
- A book can only be borrowed if a copy is available. Each loan is either open or returned.
- Books and members with loan history cannot be deleted, so the history stays complete.
- Every database query uses parameters (`?`), never string formatting.

## Endpoints

| Method | Path | Does |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/books` | List books with available copies |
| POST | `/books` | Add a book: `{"title", "author", "isbn", "copies"}` |
| GET / PUT / DELETE | `/books/{id}` | Read, change or delete one book |
| GET / POST | `/members` | List or add members: `{"name", "email"}` |
| GET / DELETE | `/members/{id}` | Read or delete one member |
| GET | `/loans` (add `?open=true` for open loans only) | List loans |
| POST | `/loans` | Borrow: `{"book_id", "member_id"}` |
| POST | `/loans/{id}/return` | Return a loan |

Errors return `{"error": "..."}` with status 400 (invalid input), 404 (not found), 405 (wrong method) or 409 (not allowed right now).

## Setup and usage

From this folder:

```bash
python server.py
```

Then, in another terminal:

```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/books -d "{\"title\": \"Dune\", \"author\": \"Frank Herbert\", \"isbn\": \"9780441172719\", \"copies\": 2}"
curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/books
```

Press `Ctrl+C` to stop the server. Data is saved in `library.db` in this folder.

## Tests

```bash
python -m unittest discover -v
```

The tests use a temporary in-memory database, so they never touch `library.db`.

## Limitations

- Development server only: it runs on this computer, without HTTPS or user accounts, and handles one request at a time.
- No search, pagination or due dates for loans.
